g the centre; the position is level (about +0.2). }) 5... Bc7 { [%csl Gc7][%cal Gd6c7] } 6. O-O { [%csl Gg1][%cal Ge1g1] } 6... Nf6 { [%csl Gf6][%cal Gg8f6] } 7. c3 { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gc2c3] } 7... O-O { [%csl Gg8][%cal Ge8g8] } 8. Qc2 { [%csl Gc2][%cal Gd1c2] } 8... Re8 $15 { Black maintains his spacious advantage. } { [%csl Ge8,Ge5][%cal Gf8e8,Ge8e5] } 9. b4 $15 { White finds play on the queenside. } { [%csl Gb4][%cal Gb2b4] } 9... a5 $15 { Black must not allow a White counter-attack on the queenside. } { [%csl Ga5][%cal Ga7a5] } 10. bxa5 { [%csl Ga5][%cal Gb4a5] } 10... Bxa5 { [%csl Ga5][%cal Gc7a5] } 11. Rd1 { [%csl Gd1][%cal Gf1d1] } 11... Nbd7 $15 { Black's centre is manageable. } { [%csl Gd7,Ge5,Gd5,Gc6,Gb7][%cal Gb8d7,Gd7e5,Gf6d5,Gc6d5,Gb7d5] } 12. Nf1 Nf8 $15 { With ideas of Ng6 to support the e5 pawn without having to block the light square bishop. } { [%csl Gf8,Gg6][%cal Gd7f8,Gf8g6] } 13. Ng3 h6 $15 { This prevents any hasty pin. } { [%csl Gh6,Gg5][%cal Gh7h6,Gc1g5,Gf3g5] } 14. h3 Ng6 { [%csl Gg6][%cal Gf8g6] } 15. Rb1 { [%csl Gb1][%cal Ga1b1] } 15... Bc7 $17 { [Engine verdict: a modest Black edge (-1.0).] [%csl Gc7][%cal Ga5c7] } 16. Rb2 (16. Nh2 b6 17. Ra1 c5 18. a4 Bd7 19. Bd2 Nf4 20. Bf3 Bc6 { another way to meet it (about -0.9) }) 16... Ra7 17. Nh2 Nf4 18. Bf3 Ra6 19. a4 c5 $17 { Black has everything going: the knights head for f4, the rooks double on the a-file and ...c5 prepares ...d4 and ...Bd7. White's pieces are passive and the queenside pawn storm with b4 has run out of steam. Your plan is to keep improving (...Bd7, ...Rea8) and only open the position when it favours you (about -0.9). } *


