Gb5b7,Gg2b7,Ge2b5] } 18... f4? $18 { Attack is the best defence. Probably Stoumbou thought that she can capture whites dark square bishop if white should take the g6 bishop. But then she missed that Makka could play the move Nh8 taking the rook. } { [%csl Gf4][%cal Gh4g6,Gf4e3,Gg6h8,Gf5f4] } 19. Nxg6 { [%csl Gg6][%cal Gh4g6] } 19... hxg6 $18 { Opening the h-file.   WATCH OUT: Qxc3 looks like a natural, tempting try for Black here (it's a capture/check a club player would consider), but it's not just worse, it's losing outright for Black: after Qxb7#, White forces mate. WATCH OUT: exd4 looks like a natural, tempting try for Black here (it's a capture/check a club player would consider), but it leaves Black clearly worse (roughly -8.8 from Black's own side of the board), after: Bxf4 Ne5 Nxe5 Bxe5 Bxe5 a6 } { [%csl Gg6][%cal Gh8h2,Gh7g6] } 20. gxf4 { [%csl Gf4][%cal Gg3f4] } 20... Nb8 $18 { Sacrificing the pawn on e5? } { [%csl Gb8][%cal Gd7b8] } 21. Rfb1 $18 { Protecting the queen. } { [%csl Gb1][%cal Gb1b5,Gf1b1] } 21... Nc6 $18 { It is unclear why Black did not take the d4 pawn; the f4 pawn could not be taken because the recapture would come with an attack on the queen. } { [%csl Gf4,Gc6][%cal Ge5d4,Ge3f4,Gf4c7,Gb8c6] } 22. fxe5 $18 { Improving the pawn structure. } { [%csl Ge5,Gd4,Gc3][%cal Gf4e5] } 22... f6 { [%csl Gf6][%cal Gf7f6] } 23. a6 $18 { threatening a checkmate in only a few turns. } { [%csl Gb1,Gb7,Ga6][%cal Gg2h3,Gh3c8,Gb5b7,Gc7b7,Ga5a6] } 23... b6 { [%csl Gb6][%cal Gb7b6] } 24. Qxc6 $18 { The queen is protected by the bishop on g7. } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gg2c6,Gb5c6] } 24... Qxc6 $18 { Black is forced to take the queen } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gc7c6] } 25. Bxc6 { [%csl Gc6][%cal Gg2c6] } 25... fxe5 { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gf6e5] } 26. d5 { [%csl Gd5][%cal Gd5c6,Gd4d5] } 26... Rh3 { [%csl Gh3][%cal Gh8h3] } 27. Bxb6 $18 { 1-0 White wins. } { [%csl Gb6][%cal Gc5b6] } 1-0


